        {
          "source_line": 55,
          "tex": "Let $S$ be a scheme and let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$.\nIn this chapter and the following we will write $X \\times_S X$\nfor the product of $X$ with itself (in the category of algebraic\nspaces over $S$), instead of $X \\times X$. The reason is that we\nwant to avoid confusion when changing base schemes, as in\nSpaces, Section \\ref{spaces-section-change-base-scheme}."
        }
      ],
